    "description": "The Kelowna and Vernon Hospitals project is a British Columbia hospital PPP spanning patient care expansions at the Kelowna and Vernon campuses and related academic facilities. Its end users are patients, clinicians, and the public health system rather than commercial customers. The model is asset-heavy and availability-based, reflecting long-term public-sector hospital infrastructure payments. Public materials describe the project as including patient care towers, a clinical academic campus, and parking infrastructure, with completion in 2018. Project-level revenue and equity percentages were not publicly disclosed in the reviewed sources. The investment is associated with Jura Acquisition, the vehicle backed by funds managed by Equitix and Dalmore, following the take-private of John Laing Infrastructure Fund.",
